Click a period on the History tab, or Open this period after clicking a point on the chart, to open one Metric's page for one period, such as /metrics/churn-rate/2026-03-01 (a month may also be written 2026-03). The Metric's name on it leads to the Metric, and on a phone it is large enough to tap with a thumb. The page shows:
the Metric, the period and its state (for example Locked or Waiting for Approval), with the value in large figures; after a Correction, the value it was submitted as is struck through;
History: every step of that period's value in order, with the person, the channel and…

Archive… puts aside a Metric you no longer track, without deleting anything. Confirm with Archive the Metric. If a Total you may change adds it up, the same dialog asks up to which period it counts there (proposed: the last one it has a value for). An Archived Metric:
keeps its description, values, history and Versions, and its page stays readable, marked Archived with the day it was archived;
asks for nothing: its Workflow skips it, so no Prompt, reminder or Escalation goes out for it, and Ask me now is gone;
takes no values: a value sent for it by the form link, email, Slack, Telegram, the…

Owners and Admins see Update from a file… on each installed Pack (an Owner, when it holds Themes). Choose the newer file: its version must be higher than the one installed. Ziffr checks the whole file and lists every item with what the new version does to it (added, changed, removed or the same) and what happens here:
an item nobody changed is replaced by the new version;
an item you changed, such as a renamed Dashboard Template or an edited Theme, stays as you made it, and the new version is offered beside it;
an item the new version drops is removed, or kept without being marked as from the…
